---
const tapeName = "tape://20.2.272.tape";
const mirrorRoot = "https://20-2-272.tapekit.org/";
const versionedPrefix = "https://20-2-272.tapekit.org/civicord/uk-2024-25/holborn-and-st-pancras/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11";
const versionedIndex = `${versionedPrefix}/index.html`;
const verifyPage = `${versionedPrefix}/verify.html`;
const manifestUrl = `${versionedPrefix}/manifest.json`;
const publicGuide = "https://github.com/sneldao/civicord/blob/main/docs/deweb-mirror.md";
const manifestSha256 = "2993bbce8d018be26a1664abcb586f5b034cbb6fd7732c4a17e056e877465901";
const container = "0xB078da6de46795656187052322Dda3A7E249C288";
const pinnedBlock = "76865195";
const directCommand = "python3 scripts/tapeout/verify_deweb.py data/out/deweb/holborn-and-st-pancras/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11 --container 0xB078da6de46795656187052322Dda3A7E249C288 --prefix civicord/uk-2024-25/holborn-and-st-pancras/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11";
---

<section class="tapeout-mirror" aria-labelledby="tapeout-mirror-title" data-motion-evidence>
  <div class="tapeout-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="tapeout-kicker">Frozen evidence mirror</p>
      <h2 id="tapeout-mirror-title">Seven records. One independently checkable bundle.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      The canonical reading interface stays here. The mirror freezes this seven-candidate cohort —
      methodology, caveats, sources, records and hashes — so a third party can inspect the evidence
      without trusting this page or the gateway.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="verification-steps" aria-label="What was verified">
    <li class="verify-step">
      <b>7 frozen files</b>
      <span>methodology, caveats, sources, records and manifest</span>
    </li>
    <li class="verify-step">
      <b>SHA-256 matched</b>
      <span>size and payload hash checked for every file</span>
    </li>
    <li class="verify-step">
      <b>2 direct RPC reads</b>
      <span>pinned block <code>{pinnedBlock}</code>; gateway response not used</span>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="tapeout-fingerprint" aria-label="Bundle fingerprint">
    <span>manifest</span>
    <code>{manifestSha256.slice(0, 18)}…{manifestSha256.slice(-10)}</code>
    <button type="button" data-copy-text={manifestSha256} data-copy-done="Manifest hash copied.">Copy full hash</button>
    <span class="pair-copy-status" role="status"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="record-actions tapeout-actions" aria-label="Open the mirror and verification material">
    <a class="btn-primary" href={versionedIndex} rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the fixed version</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href={verifyPage} rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect verification</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href={publicGuide} rel="noopener noreferrer">Verification guide</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href={mirrorRoot} rel="noopener noreferrer">Mirror root</a>
  </div>

  <details class="tapeout-direct">
    <summary>Advanced chain and publication details</summary>
    <dl class="tapeout-facts">
      <div>
        <dt>Bundle version</dt>
        <dd><code>audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11</code></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Tape name</dt>
        <dd><code>{tapeName}</code></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Container</dt>
        <dd><code>{container}</code></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Manifest</dt>
        <dd><a href={manifestUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">manifest.json</a></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Verification report</dt>
        <dd><code>data/out/deweb/verification/audit-2026-09-07-export-2026-11-b078da6de4.json</code></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Trust boundary</dt>
        <dd>two configured RPC operators; not perfect censorship resistance</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p>
      The independent check read file bytes from X Layer at one pinned block, checked the pinned
      SiteRegistry implementation, and compared size plus SHA-256 for all seven frozen files:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{directCommand}</code></pre>
  </details>

  <p class="muted tapeout-limits">
    Limits stay attached to the evidence: the container holder can technically write paths, so Civicord follows an
    append-only versioned publication policy. Cite the fixed versioned URL and manifest hash. DNS errors, redirects
    and HTTP 403 are technical classes, not allegations of intent. Bulk claim diffs are omitted because their scope
    caveats need review.
  </p>
</section>
